      "writtenOn": "2025-12-02T20:45:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm, one alternative I can think of is to make it such that the `Destroy` actually takes priority and the in-flight operation fails instead? I\u0027m not actually sure how feasible that would be since that would effectively allow racing in the backend impls which could result in UB... Though maybe that\u0027s tolerable since anyone calling `Destroy` on different threads are probably required to do external synchronization anyways?\n\nI\u0027m imagining that functions that cause a transition form state A-\u003eInsideOp via an atomic exchange would also then need to do a transition from InsideOp-\u003eB with another atomic exchange which could fail (and maybe do a cleanup?)\n\nTo be fair though, I\u0027m also not sure if that\u0027s easier than just the atomic wait for the previous operation to finish before destroying. From briefly looking at the code, I feel like doing the wait might actually be easier?",
